# esbuild writes each bundled module's path, relative to the build directory,
# into review-ledger.bundle.js as a comment and a module key. The package was
# built inside a workspace whose store sat two levels up, so the vendored bytes
# say `../../node_modules/.pnpm/...`. Keeping the store at that same relative
# location keeps every build byte-comparable with the committed bundles instead
# of rewriting four inert lines. The store lands in the repo root's node_modules/.
virtual-store-dir=../../node_modules/.pnpm
